  "content": {
    "_uid": "d727d2bc-79fc-03cb-b656-a35d6e3038ed",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "274db72f-14eb-1e7a-d2c8-ce6b10822c75",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "This course offered by The Physiotherapy Department and Nursing Education Services, in collaboration with CIME, helps learners to be aware of their own physical health while helping patients to avoid complications of bed-rest and preventable injuries through incorrect moving and handling technique.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "This simulation-based workshop for nurses and physiotherapists enabled them to become knowledgeable and competent in the optimal handling and ambulation of post-procedure orthopaedic patients. By definition these patients will have compromised ambulation and requires some assistance. It encouraged learners to work with improved co-ordination that would be transferrable from simulated to real world situations, thereby improving efficiency and effectiveness that should result in improved patient outcomes.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
